David Damerell <damer...@chiark.greenend.org.uk> wrote:
>
> When you are in the endgame, level_difficulty() is the average of the
> sanctum's depth and your XL. Of course this makes no difference to traps,
> since that number is high enough to permit any trap and trap generation in
> the endgame is peculiar anyway; but it does mean that monster difficulty
> in the endgame, which uses the average of XL and level_difficulty(), is
> weighted 3 times as strongly to XL as to the Sanctum's depth. I wonder if
> that means that the conventional wisdom, that low XL cannot prevent
> Archons and other nasties in the endgame, is wrong?

The sanctum is depth 50-60.  Archons are DIF 26.  Arch-liches
are DIF 29 - The only monster that has normal random
generation that I could find that was higher.  For comparison
adult dragons are DIF 20.

With a maximum depth dungeon of 60 (if I read the spoiler
correctly) you could get there at XP 1 for an average of
(XP + lev)/2 of 30.  Both Archons and arch-Liches can be
created no matter your level.

With a minimum depth dungeon of 50 you could get there
at XP 1 for an average of (XP + lev)/2 of 25.  This misses
Archon random generation.  The dungeon could still have
iron golems or mastadons at 22, master Liches at 21
though.  But all you need is XP 2 and Archons can be
generated.

I don't know anyone skilled enough to survive the Sanctum
at XP 1 and even getting there would depend on the random
dungeon generation to give you the minimum depth dungeon.
Archons can be generated.  If your purpose in avoiding
leveling really is to not see an Archon it doesn't look like it
can work.

Avoiding leveling to avoid Archons makes some sense before
you find the VS.  After you find the VS not so much.  But as
long as you're mean enough once you've found the VS to
survive it no longer matters.  Also, once you have the Amulet
most players avoid combat and run for the planes.


